  "text": "To find the sum of all integer bases \\( b > 9 \\) for which \\( 17_b \\) is a divisor of \\( 97_b \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the numbers from base \\( b \\) to base 10:**\n   - \\( 17_b = 1 \\cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \\)\n   - \\( 97_b = 9 \\cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \\)\n\n2. **Set up the divisibility condition:**\n   - We need \\( b + 7 \\) to divide \\( 9b + 7 \\). This means that there exists an integer \\( k \\) such that:\n     \\[\n     9b + 7 = k(b + 7)\n     \\]\n   - Rearrange the equation to isolate \\( b \\):\n     \\[\n     9b + 7 = kb + 7k\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     9b - kb = 7k - 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     b = \\frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Determine the values of \\( k \\) that make \\( b \\) an integer and \\( b > 9 \\):**\n   - For \\( b \\) to be an integer, \\( \\frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \\) must be an integer.\n   - We need to find the values of \\( k \\) such that \\( 9 - k \\) divides \\( 7(k - 1) \\).\n\n4. **Test possible values of \\( k \\):**\n   - Let's test values of \\( k \\) starting from 1 and moving upwards:\n     - For \\( k = 1 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(1 - 1)}{9 - 1} = \\frac{0}{8} = 0 \\quad (\\text{not valid since } b > 9)\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 2 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(2 - 1)}{9 - 2} = \\frac{7}{7} = 1 \\quad (\\text{not valid since } b > 9)\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 3 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(3 - 1)}{9 - 3} = \\frac{14}{6} = \\frac{7}{3} \\quad (\\text{not valid since } b \\text{ must be an integer})\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 4 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(4 - 1)}{9 - 4} = \\frac{21}{5} \\quad (\\text{not valid since } b \\text{ must be an integer})\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 5 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(5 - 1)}{9 - 5} = \\frac{28}{4} = 7 \\quad (\\text{not valid since } b > 9)\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 6 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(6 - 1)}{9 - 6} = \\frac{35}{3} \\quad (\\text{not valid since } b \\text{ must be an integer})\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 7 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(7 - 1)}{9 - 7} = \\frac{42}{2} = 21 \\quad (\\text{valid since } b > 9)\n       \\]\n     - For \\( k = 8 \\):\n       \\[\n       b = \\frac{7(8 - 1)}{9 - 8} = \\frac{49}{1} = 49 \\quad (\\text{valid since } b > 9)\n       \\]\n\n5. **Sum the valid values of \\( b \\):**\n   - The valid values of \\( b \\) are 21 and 49.\n   - The sum of these values is:\n     \\[\n     21 + 49 = 70\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{70}\n\\]",
